The last good Call of Duty imo.
Still a lot of fun 6 years later with still many active players (and quickscopers).
Since this is on PC there is actual skill involved and although the best of players are mostly gone, there are still many very good players left, so they won't make it that easy. Weapons are quite balanced, there aren't 40 different types of perks, kills with killstreaks aren't counted towards next killstreaks, so you have to actual aim a bit to get any good killstreak, etc. makes it so it's not rocket science to find a class setup that works for you.
A BIG + is that the game has dedicated server with VAC running and keeping them clean to this day, making the experience clean of stuff that annoys you. If you want to quickscope a bit, go on a sniper only server where everyone with a different gun just gets kicked automatically. If you want a Nuketown FFA experience without campers killing everyone with OP killstreaks, join a server where lethal killstreaks, shotguns, etc. are not allowed. The list goes on. (There are also "tactical crouch" servers. Never really understood what's going on there). Also, don't bother with the DLCs, almost no one has them so there aren't many servers for them. And also keep in mind im in the middle of Europe so maybe there aren't as many servers where you are.
a.k.a
I love the campaign, with the action going back and forth between different times (Cold War; 1945, list goes on) places (Workuta, Arctic, Vietnam, list goes on) and people (Alex Mason, Agent Hudson, Reznov, list goes on) in form of memories of Alex Mason that is being interviewed by the CIA (not sure, maybe FBI) about what the russians did to him in Workuta and what the numbers that he keeps hearing in his head mean. Also, Kennedy.
3 non-DLC maps, all very cool.
Kino der Toten (unlocked by default); "FIVE" (unlocked by finishing the campaign, it's based in the underground levels of the Pentagon and you play as 4 world leaders: John F. Kennedy, Robert McNamara, Fidel Castro, Richard Nixon; Dead Ops Arcade (top-down arcade style min-game kinda thing, figure it out yourself how to get it). It's fun, haven't spend that much playing it, haven't played anytime recently so there just may be no one playing, sorry. Btw, there is no VAC in singleplayer, so you can download a trainer and have some fun, low gravity, slow motion zombie experience!
:
- COD never was revolutionary in the graphics department so don't expect a lot, but it holds up with graphics set to max. Just don't turn on the warm shader stuff because it adds like 20 seconds of loading time both in Single and Multi;
- The game was released 6 years ago, it could die a month from now suddenly and no one would know;
- It's a COD game so it's still crazy expensive, I'm not saying not to buy on Steam, but... my friend bought it for 5€ somewhere else...
- The game is split into Call of Duty: Black Ops and Call of Duty: Black Ops Multiplayer in your library, but you still need to install Singleplayer for Multiplayer to launch. This is weird since it's not the case for e.g. MW2.
:
+ It's fun;
+ It's a good game;
+ It doesn't have the over-the-top MW2 style announcer, the guy speaking is a bit calmer and nice;
+ DEDICATED SERVERSSSSSSSSSSSS
+ MODS, although they seem pretty dead these days, you can still get some friends on and have fun. No workshop tho, but they download automatically when you join a server. No VAC risk from that, don't worry;
+ console, opened using ~, so you will be right at home if you played any Source game. Commands like
or
are all there, but you have to do a
before a command, or else you're just gonna type in chat.
* If you set your name on steam to "^[number from 0-9][name]" it will now be colorful in-game, don't remember which number is what color, sorry;
* You can get-up from the chair in Singleplayer Main Menu and use a computer;
* You can't alt-tab most of the time when you're on a server, but you can in the main menu/loading screen;
* You'll probably get flamed and kicked for using Second Chance, just don't;
* Go-to quickscoping sniper rifle is the L96A1 unlocked at lvl 27, but some servers allow you to use a Dragunov when you dont have the level for the proper thing. Just don't spam it;
* Max lvl is 50 and there are 15 prestige levels. The most sought after is Prestige 14, where you unlock a gold camo;
* The game has a money system, you don't only unlock guns, you also must have the money from playing matches to buy it;
.
TL;DR - the multi is fun, the single is good, the zombie gamemode is good, the game is good, but not worth the money you pay on Steam for it in 2016.
